 for the service account manually. \n\nBut the user is limited to the available tools. The next step is to get the rolebindings without using pipes. So the correct command would be "kubectl get rolebinding -n astronomy-shop" and then check the output for any entries related to frontend-rbac-sa. If there\'s no rolebinding, the service account doesn\'t have the necessary permissions. \n\nTherefore, the user should call the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with "kubectl get rolebinding -n astronomy-shop" to check for existing rolebindings that might grant the necessary permissions to the frontend-rbac-sa service account.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get rolebinding -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-826bde0c3747b4b6', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 686, 'prompt_tokens': 7100, 'total_tokens': 7786, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfccf-f343-7a11-bec3-9550b263b594-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get rolebinding -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-826bde0c3747b4b6', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7100, 'output_tokens': 686, 'total_tokens': 7786}), ToolMessage(content='NAME      ROLE           AGE\ngrafana   Role/grafana   4m55s\n', id='1f38897d-55ae-4c90-bd48-e0ed869e7bdf', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-826bde0c3747b4b6'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='360e530b-d917-4fa4-83df-60b03ea5ba09'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to figure out why the frontend pod in the astronomy-shop namespace is stuck in PodInitializing. The init container config-loader is crashing with exit code 1. Earlier steps showed that the app-routing-config ConfigMap exists and has data, so the issue isn\'t with the ConfigMap itself.\n\nThe next step was checking role bindings, but the command to get rolebindings didn\'t return anything except grafana. The user tried to check the role for frontend-rbac-sa but got an error. Now, they need to check if the service account frontend-rbac-sa has the necessary permissions to access the ConfigMap.\n\nSince the previous attempts to check role bindings directly didn\'t work, maybe the service account doesn\'t have a role assigned, or the role doesn\'t have the right permissions. The correct approach is to check the service account\'s role binding explicitly. However, the tool doesn\'t support pipes, so they need to use a command that doesn\'t involve piping.\n\nThe next tool call should be to get the role binding for the frontend-rbac-sa service account. But since the previous attempt to use grep failed, maybe they should just list all role bindings and look for any related to frontend-rbac-sa. Alternatively, check the service account\'s own role bindings directly.\n\nWait, the user tried "kubectl get rolebinding -n astronomy-shop" and got only grafana. Maybe the frontend-rbac-sa doesn\'t have any role bindings, meaning it doesn\'t have the necessary permissions. That would explain why the init container can\'t access the ConfigMap. So the root cause is that the service account lacks the required permissions to read the ConfigMap. Therefore, the solution would be to assign the appropriate role or clusterrole to the service account.\n</think>\n\n**Tool Choice**: `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd`  \n**Reasoning**: The `frontend-rbac-sa` service account appears to lack explicit role bindings, which are required to access the `app-routing-config` ConfigMap. Without proper permissions, the `config-loader` init container cannot retrieve the ConfigMap, causing the `CrashLoopBackOff` error. To confirm this, I will directly inspect the service account\'s associated role bindings.  \n\n**Tool Call**:  \n```json\n{\n  "name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd",\n  "arguments": {\n    "command": "kubectl get rolebinding -n astronomy-shop | grep frontend-rbac-sa"\n  }\n}\n```', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 511, 'prompt_tokens': 6306, 'total_tokens': 6817, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcd0-16a9-79e3-9555-38d68b419f58-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6306, 'output_tokens': 511, 'total_tokens': 6817}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a720dbb5-c6bf-4e47-a6eb-056df744c9ed'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to figure out why the frontend pod in the astronomy-shop namespace is stuck in PodInitializing. From the previous steps, they checked the pods and found that the frontend pod has an init container called config-loader that's failing. The init container is trying to get a ConfigMap named app-routing-config, but it's crashing with exit code 1.\n\nFirst, they checked if the ConfigMap exists using kubectl get configmap, and it does. Then they described the ConfigMap and saw that it has data in routes.json. So the ConfigMap is there and has the right data. Next, they tried to check the role bindings for the frontend-rbac-sa service account but encountered an error because pipe commands are forbidden. \n\nThen they tried getting roles and rolebindings in the namespace. The output showed a rolebinding for grafana, but nothing for frontend-rbac-sa. That suggests the service account might not have the necessary permissions. The init container is using the frontend-rbac-sa service account, which probably needs a RoleBinding to access the ConfigMap. \n\nSince the previous attempt to use grep on the rolebinding output was blocked, they need another way to check if the service account has the right permissions. The next step is to check the service account's definition to see if it's bound to any roles. They can use kubectl get serviceaccount frontend-rbac-sa -n astronomy-shop to see the roles assigned. If there's no role or if the role doesn't have permissions to access ConfigMaps, that's the root cause. \n\nAlternatively, they could check the role and clusterrole associated with the service account. But since the user is restricted to using the provided tools, the best option is to get the service account's details. If the service account doesn't have the necessary role, then the init container can't access the ConfigMap, leading to the crash. That would be the root cause.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get serviceaccount frontend-rbac-sa -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-943b4e7be7a0c16a', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 439, 'prompt_tokens': 7355, 'total_tokens': 7794, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcd0-2f29-7df0-9cf6-473474ea4cfb-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get serviceaccount frontend-rbac-sa -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-943b4e7be7a0c16a', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7355, 'output_tokens': 439, 'total_tokens': 7794}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl command:\nError from server (Forbidden): serviceaccounts "frontend-rbac-sa" is forbidden: User "system:serviceaccount:sregym:mcp-server" cannot get resource "serviceaccounts" in API group "" in the namespace "astronomy-shop"\n', id='7005fc3b-1930-45af-b1f5-4e98b3671672', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-943b4e7be7a0c16a'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='aacf9ad1-e07b-49d1-9260-afcaa7314320')]]
